harness_limitations[4]: "Module lookup is executed from the repository root; tq cases use explicit confined -L roots, while jq path-substitution cases retain the documented HOME and $ORIGIN forms.",The child HOME override is confined to the owned fixture tree so user startup files cannot affect results.,The compatibility harness compares result sequences semantically; tq's default TOON Text Sequence output is intentionally left unmodified.,jq's empty-path termination and tq's rejection of empty or unsupported path substitutions are retained as observed compatibility differences.
coverage_notes[33]{id,source_line,kind,query,input,disposition,reason,evidence_case_id}:
  modules.system,16,prose-capability,"import \"basic\" as b; b::value","null",new,The prose introduces the module system; an imported fixture provides an executable witness.,manual.modules.import
  modules.search-path-directives,18,prose-capability,"include \"included\"; included_value","null",new,The prose names import/include search-path directives; the include case exercises the directive with an explicit root.,manual.modules.include
  modules.path-substitutions,20,prose-capability,"import \"basic\" as b; b::value","null",adapted,"The path substitutions are exercised by dedicated dot, HOME/tilde, and executable-origin cases; tq uses explicit confined-root adapters for its restrictions.",null
  modules.path-tilde,22,prose-capability,"import \"home\" as h; h::value","null",adapted,jq uses a child-only HOME pointing at the owned fixture and ~/.jq; tq uses the equivalent explicit root because it does not expand tilde roots.,manual.modules.path-tilde
  modules.path-origin,24,prose-capability,"import \"foo\" as f; f::value","null",adapted,jq uses $ORIGIN-relative fixture lookup; tq uses an explicit confined root because executable-origin substitution is not supported.,manual.modules.path-origin
  modules.path-dot,26,prose-capability,"import \"basic\" as b; b::value","null",adapted,The jq top-level ./ root is literal; tq receives the canonical equivalent explicit root.,manual.modules.path-dot
  modules.path-dot-including,26,prose-capability,"import \"main\" as m; m::value","null",new,"A module containing include \"./child\" verifies that dot resolves relative to the including file.",manual.modules.path-dot-including
  modules.import-search-path,28,prose-capability,"import \"meta/consumer\" as c; c::value","null",new,"A consumer module imports its helper with constant search metadata, exercising the prefixed dependency path.",manual.modules.import-search
  modules.default-search-description,30,prose-capability,"[\"~/.jq\", \"$ORIGIN/../lib/jq\", \"$ORIGIN/../lib\"]","null",new,The documented default path is made executable as a literal value; actual module lookup remains covered by explicit-root cases.,manual.modules.default-search-path
  modules.search-terminator,37,prose-capability,"import \"consumer\" as c; c::value","null",adapted,"jq receives an empty search element and terminates dependency lookup; tq rejects empty confined roots, so its adapter keeps only explicit non-empty roots to expose the restriction.",manual.modules.search-terminator
  modules.relative-dependency,39,prose-capability,"import \"foo/bar\" as f; f::value","null",new,Separate roots witness both foo/bar.jq and foo/bar/bar.jq resolution forms named by the prose.,null
  modules.relative-single-file,39,prose-path-pattern,"import \"foo/bar\" as f; f::value","null",new,The single-file candidate is present in the owned fixture root.,manual.modules.relative-single
  modules.relative-directory-file,39,prose-path-pattern,"import \"foo/bar\" as f; f::value","null",new,The directory-module candidate is present in a separate owned root with no competing single-file candidate.,manual.modules.relative-directory
  modules.repeated-components,41,prose-validation,"import \"foo/foo\" as f; f::value","null",new,The repeated-component prohibition is executable as a compile-error witness; tq currently accepts it and records the compatibility difference.,manual.modules.repeated-component
  modules.foo-search-example,43,prose-example,"import \"foo\" as f; f::value","null",new,Separate roots witness both foo.jq and foo/foo.jq forms from the documented -L$HOME/.jq example.,null
  modules.home-auto-source,45,prose-capability,home_value,"null",adapted,jq receives a child-only HOME whose .jq file is auto-sourced; tq remains enabled to expose its missing auto-source behavior.,manual.modules.home-auto-source
  modules.import-signature,47,prose-signature,"import \"basic\" as b; b::value","null",new,The concrete fixture instantiates the import RelativePathString as NAME signature.,manual.modules.import
  modules.import-qualification,49,prose-capability,"import \"basic\" as b; b::value","null",covered,"The qualified b::value call directly exercises the documented namespace prefix.",manual.modules.import
  modules.import-metadata,51,prose-capability,"import \"basic\" as b {\"homepage\":\"override\"}; b::value","null",new,A constant object metadata witness exercises the optional import metadata form.,manual.modules.import-metadata
  modules.import-search-metadata,53,prose-capability,"import \"meta/consumer\" as c; c::value","null",covered,The consumer's import metadata contains a relative search path used to locate helper.jq.,manual.modules.import-search
  modules.include-signature,55,prose-signature,"include \"included\"; included_value","null",new,The concrete fixture instantiates the include RelativePathString signature.,manual.modules.include
  modules.include-namespace,57,prose-capability,"include \"included\"; included_value","null",covered,The unqualified included_value call directly verifies inclusion into the caller namespace.,manual.modules.include
  modules.include-metadata,59,prose-capability,"import \"meta/include-consumer\" as c; c::value","null",new,The include fixture carries constant search metadata and resolves a helper from its parent directory.,manual.modules.include-metadata
  modules.import-json-signature,61,prose-signature,"import \"data\" as $data; $data::data","null",new,The JSON-module import signature is instantiated with an owned data.json fixture.,manual.modules.import-json
  modules.import-json-value,63,prose-capability,"import \"data\" as $data; $data::data","null",covered,"The $data::data reference directly exercises the documented data binding.",manual.modules.import-json
  modules.import-json-metadata,65,prose-capability,"import \"data\" as $data {\"homepage\":\"data\"}; $data::data","null",covered,The JSON import case uses the exact data binding while jq parses optional metadata in the same directive form.,manual.modules.import-json
  modules.import-json-search,67,prose-capability,"import \"data\" as $data; $data::data","null",covered,The data import remains rooted with an explicit search path; tq is enabled to expose its current JSON-module limitation.,manual.modules.import-json
  modules.module-signature,69,prose-signature,"import \"basic\" as b; \"basic\" | modulemeta","null",new,The basic.jq fixture begins with module metadata and is observed through modulemeta.,manual.modules.modulemeta
  modules.module-optional,71,prose-capability,"import \"basic\" as b; b::value","null",covered,The imported module operates correctly with its optional module directive.,manual.modules.import
  modules.module-constant,73,prose-validation,"import \"basic\" as b {\"homepage\": .}; b::value","null",new,A non-constant metadata expression is an executable compile-error witness for the constant-expression requirement.,manual.modules.metadata-constant
  modules.modulemeta-signature,75,prose-signature,"import \"basic\" as b; \"basic\" | modulemeta","null",new,The modulemeta filter is run after importing the named module.,manual.modules.modulemeta
  modules.modulemeta-shape,77,prose-capability,"import \"meta/consumer\" as c; \"meta/consumer\" | modulemeta","null",new,The result exposes deps (including search metadata) and defs as documented.,manual.modules.modulemeta-deps
  modules.modulemeta-program-use,79,prose-capability,"import \"basic\" as b; \"basic\" | modulemeta | {defs, deps}","null",covered,The case makes the metadata available to a subsequent jq program expression.,manual.modules.modulemeta
